---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Brift"
  description="Brift Technologies privacy policy regarding client data, site operations, and infrastructure security."
>
  <div class="py-10 sm:py-20 lg:py-24 bg-bg">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Legal Review Notice Alert -->
      <div class="mb-6 sm:mb-8 rounded-xl border border-yellow/60 bg-yellow/15 p-3.5 sm:p-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink-2">
        <strong class="font-bold text-ink">Legal Notice:</strong> This privacy policy is an initial informational draft provided for platform development. It must be formally reviewed and finalized by qualified legal counsel prior to live public deployment.
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-card-lg border border-line bg-white p-5 sm:p-10 lg:p-12 shadow-sm space-y-6 sm:space-y-8">
        <div>
          <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2">Last updated: September 2026</p>
        </div>

        <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">1. Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Brift Technologies ("Brift", "we", "our") provides construction operations management software. This policy outlines how we collect, handle, and protect data submitted through our marketing website and client-tailored platforms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">2. Information We Collect</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-muted">
            <li><strong>Lead & Inquiry Data:</strong> Contact information provided when scheduling a demo, including full name, phone number, company name, and active site counts.</li>
            <li><strong>Operational Client Data:</strong> In client software deployments, company records, site purchases, worker attendance, contractor accounts, and project media.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical Metadata:</strong> System audit logs containing IP addresses, login timestamps, and user device identifiers to preserve security and immutable audit trails.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">3. Data Isolation & Ownership</h2>
          <p>
            All operational construction data remains the exclusive property of the client company. Brift does not sell, market, or share client project financial records with third parties. Client databases are provisioned with strict logical isolation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">4. Security & Backups</h2>
          <p>
            We implement automated database backups, TLS encryption in transit, role-based access controls, and strict session management to safeguard your site records against unauthorized tampering.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">5. Contact Information</h2>
          <p>
            For questions regarding data privacy or to exercise data rights, contact us at:
            <br />
            <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:brift.official@gmail.com" class="text-blue hover:underline">brift.official@gmail.com</a>
            <br />
            <strong>Phone:</strong> +91 9037532036
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
